(95% range +0.12 to +0.26), about +2.6\u00b0F since 1886. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.65\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.36 to +0.94) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+1.07\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.68 to +1.46). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Abilene's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.01 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 25.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1941 (48.77 in); the driest, 1956 (9.78 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}